{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CejjeptYvyjf75uFHtfdV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five REVIEW-A findings are addressed. WI-580 is closed on this branch (`f98e7d3f`, trailer `WI: WI-580`).\n\n## What changed\n\n**[MAJOR] The close bar's claim** — `project-trajectory/prompts/worker.template.md:48`. I confirmed the finding by driving it: `integrate._run_bar` calls `check.py --tier all`, check.py declares `format`/`lint`/`tests+coverage` at `_kitladder.STAGE_IMPL`, and `docs/stage` reads `DevStg-Tests` — one rung below. `check.py --jobs 0` returned PASS over **14 steps, not one of them a test step**. So the brief was excusing a worker from the only suite that would have run before phase close. The brief now names the bar declared for the repo's *current rung*, names `DevStg-Impl` as where the product test step arrives, and points at check.py's step table as the one owner of what the bar runs. I deliberately did **not** ungate `tests+coverage` — that's a ladder-semantics change every adopter migrates to, so it's an owner's call.\n\n**[MAJOR] Two homes for the cadence** — the `session-protocol` skill still said \"run the full suite before claiming a slice/phase done, at close\" while `CLAUDE.md` names that skill as the authority for commit-bar-vs-gate-bar, and the skill contradicted itself two lines later. Clause deleted from all three copies; `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` \"Phase cadence\" is the single home. The deletion is the antidote — nothing new polices it.\n\n**[MINOR] The narrowed heading** — WI-579's own heading says WI-559 item 3 is *shared*, and its Done-when never claims it, so the prior round's \"discharged by WI-579\" was a self-serving narrowing. Heading restored verbatim, and rather than reclassify I **covered** the uncovered half: `test_the_false_partial_class_turns_only_on_the_close_ritual` drives the WI-540 class on one scaffold — trailers committed, specs still in `active/`, so `lane_completion` answers `({WI-201,WI-204}, set())` and `integrate.finished_branches` answers `[]` (the `_lane_close` stall arm) — and the spec move alone flips both. Mutation-checked: the pre-WI-580 trailer-alone predicate fails it.\n\n**[MINOR ×2]** `~8%` → `~6%` (7,975 of 8,500 is 6.2%; byte-neutral, baseline unchanged), and the brief's opening sentence routed through `{scripts}` — the composed render now prints `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py`.\n\n## Bar (run here, at the tip)\n\n- smoke `1551 passed, 4 skipped`; `check_smoke_budget --mode enforce` → **51.8 s vs 60 s, within**\n- `check.py --jobs 0` → `RESULT: PASS` (11 PASS, 3 work-branch freshness SKIPs)\n- `trace.py --strict-integrity` → `orphans=0 integrity=0`\n- `check_docs --stale` → OK (1372 docs, 1602 links, 0 broken)\n- focused selection (worker/review/ratchet/prompts/routing/dogfood/bootstrap) → `235 passed, 1 skipped`\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the pre-commit hook's `format` step **SKIPPED** on both commits — its interpreter is `/usr/local/bin/python3`, which has no ruff — and printed the \"A DECLARED CHECK DID NOT RUN\" banner. I ran `ruff format --check` and `ruff check` explicitly against the toolchain venv (both clean) rather than let that read as green, and recorded it in the log fragment. That's a standing lane-worktree condition, not something this WI introduced."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":131192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":445},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13327e09-90e1-45dd-941b-0d4bfb0cab91","uuid":"c2830871-fd0f-4437-bf59-6c41d69fb1cb","request_id":"req_011CejjeoxFEMDVJ2JzTz9uh"}
